      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "While it is true flying would be in a much better state with better collider physics, that promise only holds true if colliders on avatars were actually fixed. The problem is that they aren't.\n\nYou still sink through colliders when you stand on them and your rotation still snaps to the direction of the collider. This has always been the case for avatar colliders, it's just that you could counterbalance the sinking bug using the now-patched out position snapping bug.\n\nNone of these things are proper, expected behaviors of colliders, and yet neither of the above two issues were actually addressed in the aforementioned fix.\n\nI get that there's no sense asking to rollback a fix to a bug just because it was kind of cool, so if I had to ask for anything, it would be for VRChat to fix these other two collider bugs while they're at it.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
