      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5b40c40c2353645d955d3c39|full_name}: As far as I can tell it is a harmless bug.\n\nBeing that this is a medium to express creativity, to have someone who can fly, is something of a \"neat\" aspect, and to clamp down on those who wanted to give their avatar a unique feature, that's harmless to others, then it should not be treated as a bug, as it is something that brings joy.\n\n@{58c62e995865713647a7115b|full_name} I suggest least make an option in worlds to incorporate a way to prevent common means of flight, for places such as puzzle or game type worlds, but do not disable on a whole, preventing people from enjoying such aspects, because they found a way.\n\nThis is one of the beauties of player content, to give things that allow people to stand out, when they know how, even if it was not an intended feature. (Unless it is detrimental to other players)  And just allowing everyone to just fly also makes it so it's not special, degrading the value.  The way this is heading it's an all or nothing.  Everyone can fly in a world, or not... leaving less for creativity.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
